      "A",
      "\\mathcal C_n",
      "\\mathcal C_n^{\\mathrm{RJ}}"
    ],
    "justification": "Vanishing external Gaussian jitter makes null calibration exact throughout the bounded ambient class without an influence-covariance eigenvalue condition.",
    "gap": "A direct uniform-integrability argument makes estimated-influence covariance replacement negligible relative to the squared jitter scale.",
    "consumer": "The result supplies an implementable covariance-adaptive confidence set, but makes no expected-length or diameter optimality claim.",
    "id": "thm:resolve-f367224d6b4e1796a7b2",
